IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc8-nouns`
IMPORT `roc8-order-36`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 36: TESTS.  Every expected value is written from the text of the paragraph
-- named beside it, before running.  The "last day" is a made-up date standing in for O 3 r 3's count (S-T1).

`o 36 test d1` MEANS Date 1 3 2026
`o 36 test d10` MEANS Date 10 3 2026
`o 36 test d15` MEANS Date 15 3 2026
`o 36 test d16` MEANS Date 16 3 2026
`o 36 test d20` MEANS Date 20 3 2026

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 36 r 2(2) supporting affidavit`
`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` MEANS `o 36 r 2(2) supporting affidavit` WITH
    `o 36 r 2(2)(a) it exhibits the adjudication determination (the original or a copy)` IS a
    `o 36 r 2(2)(a) it exhibits the contract to which the adjudication determination relates (the original or a copy)` IS b
    `o 36 r 2(2)(b) it states the name and the usual or last known place of business of the applicant` IS c
    `o 36 r 2(2)(b) it states the name and the usual or last known place of business of the debtor` IS d
    `o 36 r 2(2)(c) it states the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` IS e

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 36 r 3(1) supporting affidavit`
`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` MEANS `o 36 r 3(1) supporting affidavit` WITH
    `o 36 r 3(1)(a) it has exhibited to it a copy of the adjudication determination and the contract to which the adjudication determination relates` IS a
    `o 36 r 3(1)(a) it has exhibited to it any other document relied on by the applicant` IS b
    `o 36 r 3(1)(b) it states the grounds on which it is contended that the adjudication determination or judgment (as the case may be) should be set aside` IS c
    `o 36 r 3(1)(c) it sets out any evidence relied on by the applicant` IS d
    `o 36 r 3(1)(d) it is served with the application` IS e

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(1) the Act is the Building and Construction Industry Security of Payment Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(1) the Act is the Building and Construction Industry Security of Payment Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(2) the expression has the same meaning in this Order as in the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(2) the expression has the same meaning in this Order as in the Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 1(3): where an action is pending, by summons in the action; in any other case, by originating application.
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by summons in the action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by summons in the action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by summons in the action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by originating application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by originating application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application must be made by originating application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` TRUE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` TRUE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 1(3) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` FALSE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application must be made to the Registrar by originating application without notice or summons without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application must be made to the Registrar by originating application without notice or summons without notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` TRUE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` TRUE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(1) the application is made to the Registrar in a way this paragraph names` FALSE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2)(b) the person against whom enforcement is sought is called the debtor in this Rule` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2)(b) the person against whom enforcement is sought is called the debtor in this Rule` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 2(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order granting permission is drawn up as the paragraph requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order granting permission is drawn up as the paragraph requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` `o 36 r 2(3)(a) delivering a copy to the debtor personally` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` `o 36 r 2(3)(b) sending a copy to the debtor at the debtor's usual or last known place of business` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` `o 36 r 2(3)(c) such other manner as the Court may direct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` `o 36 r 2(3)(c) such other manner as the Court may direct` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(3) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` `o 36 r 2(3) some other manner` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 2(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the adjudication determination`'s `period length`) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 2(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the adjudication determination`'s `period unit`) EQUALS Days
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 2(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the adjudication determination`'s `period direction`) EQUALS `After the anchor`
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's application to set aside the adjudication determination is made in time` `o 36 test d15` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's application to set aside the adjudication determination is made in time` `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's application to set aside the adjudication determination is made in time` `o 36 test d10` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the bar: TRUE until the period has run (or the application is disposed of), FALSE after; never "has been enforced".
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination cannot yet be enforced` `o 36 test d10` `o 36 test d15` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination cannot yet be enforced` `o 36 test d15` `o 36 test d15` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination cannot yet be enforced` `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination cannot yet be enforced` `o 36 test d20` `o 36 test d15` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination cannot yet be enforced` `o 36 test d20` `o 36 test d15` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination may be enforced` `o 36 test d10` `o 36 test d15` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination may be enforced` `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(4) the adjudication determination may be enforced` `o 36 test d20` `o 36 test d15` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(5) the copy of the order served states the effect of paragraph (4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 2(5) the copy of the order served states the effect of paragraph (4)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the application must be supported by an affidavit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the application must be supported by an affidavit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(1) the affidavit has the required content` (`o 36 r 3(1) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the form of the direction to the Accountant-General` EQUALS "Form 44"
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the applicant must provide security for the unpaid portion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the applicant must provide security for the unpaid portion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided by the means the paragraph names` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided by the means the paragraph names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided by the means the paragraph names` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the amount: 100,000 adjudicated less 40,000 paid is 60,000 unpaid
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` 100000 40000 EQUALS 60000
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` 100000 0 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` 100000 100000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` 100000 120000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security provided is for the unpaid portion` 100000 40000 60000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security provided is for the unpaid portion` 100000 40000 100000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security provided is for the unpaid portion` 100000 40000 59999 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security provided is for the unpaid portion` 100000 0 100000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided at the time of filing` `o 36 test d15` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided at the time of filing` `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided at the time of filing` `o 36 test d10` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 3(3) the period for the party entitled to enforce to file an opposing affidavit`'s `period length`) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 3(3) the period for the party entitled to enforce to file an opposing affidavit`'s `period unit`) EQUALS Days
#ASSERT (`o 36 r 3(3) the period for the party entitled to enforce to file an opposing affidavit`'s `period direction`) EQUALS `After the anchor`
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application arises` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application arises` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application is filed in time` TRUE `o 36 test d15` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application is filed in time` TRUE `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application is filed in time` FALSE `o 36 test d16` `o 36 test d15` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application states the grounds` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application states the grounds` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(3) the affidavit opposing the application states the grounds` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(4) the judgment is a judgment for this Rule` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 36 r 3(4) the judgment is a judgment for this Rule` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 36 as regulative rules: traces`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on main, so each trace carries the expected outcome on the line above
-- and work/trace-check.py (run by hand, on both builds) compares.  Day 0 is the day the period starts.

-- r 2(4), the SHANT: the adjudication determination is not to be enforced until after the period.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the bar on enforcing the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor` DOES `o 36 r 2(4) enforce the adjudication determination` AT 14

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the bar on enforcing the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor` DOES `o 36 r 2(4) enforce the adjudication determination` AT 3

-- enforcing on day 15, after the period, breaches nothing.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the bar on enforcing the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor` DOES `o 36 r 2(4) enforce the adjudication determination` AT 15

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the bar on enforcing the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- r 2(4), the MAY: on main a MAY with no LEST is FULFILLED whether or not the debtor uses it, so both read FULFILLED;
-- the closing of the window is carried by the decision function, which answers JUST FALSE on day 15.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor` DOES `o 36 r 2(4) apply to set aside the adjudication determination` AT 14

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the adjudication determination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor` DOES `o 36 r 2(4) apply to set aside the adjudication determination` AT 15

-- r 3(3): the duty to file an opposing affidavit within 14 days.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 3(3) the party entitled to enforce` DOES `o 36 r 3(3) file the affidavit opposing the application` AT 14

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 36 r 3(3) the party entitled to enforce` DOES `o 36 r 3(3) file the affidavit opposing the application` AT 15

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- the duty does not arise: nothing is owed.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15
